cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EcoCompute MLCube in your work, please cite it as below, and cite the EcoCompute dataset you compare against (see the Provenance section of the README)."
title: "EcoCompute MLCube: a reproducible energy-measurement container for quantized LLM inference"
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Hongping
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0000-2529-4613
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, Changsha, Hunan, China
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/hongping-zh/ecocompute-mlcube"
abstract: >-
  Containerized measurement harness for the energy cost of quantized
  LLM inference. Measures decode-phase energy per token from direct
  power telemetry (NVIDIA NVML; mock-tested ROCm sampler pending
  real-hardware validation) and emits a schema-validated energy report.
  Reference implementation of the EcoCompute Protocol and the
  measurement tool behind the EcoCompute benchmark datasets. AMD GPUs
  are detected and reported as unavailable for energy rather than
  fitted with NVIDIA-derived curves.
keywords:
  - LLM inference
  - energy efficiency
  - quantization
  - NVML
  - ROCm
  - MLCube
  - reproducibility
  - benchmark
license: Apache-2.0
